		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Recommend adding an Always On Display (AOD) feature]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5114&amp;p=37060#p37060"><![CDATA[
The current version fails to maintain interface visibility after the screen backlight is fully disabled. It is proposed to enable persistent visualization of essential information even when the backlight is turned off. If hardware limitations exist, an intelligent backlight adjustment scheme could be implemented: Automatically activate a low-brightness mode (e.g., 10-20% backlight intensity) after screen timeout, achieving sustained display through dynamic power consumption control. This approach would maintain persistent visibility of critical information while ensuring battery endurance.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5109">BI1OFX</a> — Sat May 10, 2025 4:29 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
